# Local data and derived medical-data artifacts.
#
# The two checkpoint directories below are the defaults, but CHECKPOINT_DIR is an
# environment variable and can point anywhere, including inside this repository. The
# artifacts it receives are model weights and the split CSVs, and those CSVs carry a
# Patient ID column and image paths. Missing one of them is not a tidiness problem in a
# medical repository, so the patterns below are by shape as well as by location.
data/
checkpoints*/
logs/
temp_*.csv
*_fixed_train.csv
*_fixed_val.csv
*_fixed_test.csv
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# ai-radiologist: model weights and image corpora are redistributed by their
# owners, not from here. The weights are a 28 MB TorchXRayVision checkpoint that
# the loader fetches on demand; demo_images holds NIH ChestX-ray14 radiographs,
# which NIH distributes under its own terms.
ai-radiologist/models/
ai-radiologist/demo_images/
ai-radiologist/results/
ai-radiologist/eval/scores.json

# Python environments and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
